Skylanders player kit (@PLATFORM@)
==================================

This kit builds Skylanders Spyro's Adventure, Giants, Swap Force, Trap Team, SuperChargers and Imaginators (all Xbox 360), on your own machine from your own disc image; Arkeyan-Builder recognises which game the disc is. It contains no game code and no game file: the game's code and shaders are translated from
your disc here, and the result is for your own use only. Never share the built game or its work folder.

Normally Arkeyan Launcher runs Arkeyan-Builder for you. By hand:

    Arkeyan-Builder --iso <your disc .iso> --out <game folder> [--jobs N] [--toolchain <folder>]

It prints one event per line (@step, @progress, @log, @error, @done) and ends with "@done <path of the game>".
A second run only redoes what changed. Work files stay in <game folder>/arkeyan-work (existing ssabuild-work folders are reused in place; about 2-3 GB; delete it
once the game runs if you need the space, the next build will then start over).

Windows 10 (1903 or later) or 11, x64:
- if SmartScreen warns about the launcher or Arkeyan-Builder: More info, then Run anyway;
- internet for the first build: Arkeyan-Builder downloads the llvm-mingw 20260922 compiler (190 MB, from
  github.com/mstorsjo/llvm-mingw, checked against its SHA-256) into %APPDATA%\Skylanders\toolchains
  (about 750 MB once extracted); Arkeyan-Builder downloads and unpacks it itself, no other program is started for that;
- about 5 GB free next to the game folder, 8 GB of RAM or more;
- the first build takes 15-45 minutes depending on the CPU;
- a GPU with a Vulkan 1.2 driver (any recent NVIDIA, AMD or Intel driver), else Direct3D 12;
- an Xbox 360 portal needs Windows' own WinUSB driver, once (nothing to download): Device Manager, right-click the portal
  ("Spyro Portal", or an unknown device), Update driver, Browse my computer, Let me pick, Universal Serial Bus devices,
  WinUsb Device, then unplug it and plug it in again. An Xbox One portal needs nothing;
- a Wii, PlayStation or PC portal works on Windows' own driver or on WinUSB; on libusbK or libusb0 (Zadig), the launcher's
  portal Test shows the way back (Device Manager, Uninstall device with "Attempt to remove the driver for this device",
  then if it comes back: pnputil /enum-drivers and pnputil /delete-driver oemNN.inf /uninstall /force, as administrator).

macOS (Apple silicon): Xcode with its Metal toolchain (xcodebuild -downloadComponent MetalToolchain on Xcode 26+).
The launcher and Arkeyan-Builder are not notarized: on macOS 15 or later, the first time, try to open it, then
System Settings > Privacy & Security > Open Anyway.

Linux, x86_64 (Ubuntu 22.04 or later, Fedora, Arch, SteamOS 3.5 or later on the Steam Deck; glibc 2.34 or later):
- no root and no development package: Arkeyan-Builder downloads the zig 0.17.0 compiler (55 MB, from ziglang.org, checked
  against its SHA-256) into ~/.local/share/Skylanders/toolchains (about 410 MB once extracted, plus about 100 MB the first
  build adds there) with curl (or wget), tar and xz, which every desktop has; the shader compiler (dxc) needs
  libstdc++ (GCC 11 or later) and zlib, also on every desktop;
- about 6 GB free next to the game folder, 8 GB of RAM or more; the first build takes 15-45 minutes;
- to play: a Vulkan driver (Mesa or NVIDIA; libvulkan.so.1), X11 or Wayland and PipeWire, PulseAudio or ALSA;
- the portal: /dev/hidraw* and /dev/bus/usb/* belong to root, so the portal needs udev rules once (it is the only
  step that needs sudo; on the Steam Deck, set a password with passwd first). The first line is for the Wii, Wii U,
  PlayStation and PC portals, the other two for the Xbox 360 and Xbox One portals (1430:1F17, 1430:09AA). In a terminal:

    printf '%s\n' 'SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", ATTRS{idVendor}=="1430", ATTRS{idProduct}=="0150", MODE="0660", TAG+="uaccess"' 'SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ATTRS{idVendor}=="1430", MODE="0660", TAG+="uaccess"' 'SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ATTRS{idVendor}=="24c6", ATTRS{idProduct}=="fa00", MODE="0660", TAG+="uaccess"' | sudo tee /etc/udev/rules.d/70-skylanders-portal.rules
    sudo udevadm control --reload-rules && sudo udevadm trigger

  then unplug the portal and plug it in again. Without them the game's log says "Linux needs this udev rule". An Xbox
  portal also needs libusb-1.0 (the libusb-1.0-0 package; most desktops have it).

In this kit:
- Arkeyan-Builder: the build driver; bin/XenonRecomp and bin/XenosRecomp: the code and shader translators (separate
  programs); dxc (DirectX Shader Compiler) next to XenosRecomp (libdxcompiler.so on Linux);
- lib/, include/, commands/: the prebuilt runtime (everything but the game code) and how to compile and link against it;
- config/: XenonRecomp's settings for this game; res/: fonts and notices copied next to the game;
- licenses/: LICENSE, THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md, and the source of the (L)GPL parts shipped as binaries: XenonRecomp
  (its PowerPC disassembler is GPL-2.0-or-later) and FFmpeg 8.1.2 (LGPL-2.1-or-later, also linked into Arkeyan-Builder
  for disc menu music; ffmpeg-build.sh is how the libraries were configured);
- relink/: Arkeyan-Builder objects, libraries and its link recipe for replacing FFmpeg; see relink/README.txt.

---
FR : ce kit construit le jeu sur votre machine à partir de votre propre ISO. Il ne contient rien du jeu.
Arkeyan Launcher lance Arkeyan-Builder tout seul ; à la main : Arkeyan-Builder --iso <ISO> --out <dossier du jeu>.
Windows : il faut Internet au premier lancement (téléchargement du compilateur, 190 Mo), ~5 Go libres, et
15 à 45 min pour la première construction. Linux : le compilateur zig (55 Mo) est téléchargé, sans sudo ;
le portail demande une fois la règle udev ci-dessus. Ne partagez jamais le jeu construit.
SmartScreen (Windows) : Informations complémentaires, puis Exécuter quand même. macOS 15 ou plus, la première fois :
Réglages Système > Confidentialité et sécurité > Ouvrir quand même.
